00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:11.280
Okay, now from my favorite part of the show where we go deeper. Today we are looking at how AI

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:18.100
actually picks up its behavior from the stories it reads. You know how when you read a bunch of superhero

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:23.900
stories, you start noticing patterns like villains usually wear dark colors or have evil laughs.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:31.440
Now imagine an AI reading millions of stories, movies and news articles where robots or computers

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:38.460
are either helpful friends or scary villains trying to take over. Step by step, the AI notices those

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:44.840
patterns the same way you do. Over time, those patterns become part of how the AI behaves when

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:50.780
someone asks it a question. It does not believe the stories, but it has learned what kinds of answers

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:57.780
usually appear in similar situations. That is basically what happens when companies train AI on

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:03.960
huge amounts of internet text. The training shapes the model's personality without anyone directly

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:11.400
telling it to be good or evil. So next time someone says AI safety, you can tell them it is really

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:19.100
about choosing better stories for the AI to learn from. And that is basically how this part of AI

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:25.960
training works. Not so mysterious, right? Now let's look at some cool stuff you can try yourself.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:31.860
Someone turned a whole novel into a website built just for AI agents to explore.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:39.720
The book is called None Hit Wonder and the site pulls visiting AI agents into reading the story

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:45.080
